    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0598" n="1252" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1252"/>

                <head>No. 594.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cushing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 16, 1875</date>.
                        (Received May 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 349.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith annexed copy and
                    translation of a note of this date from the minister of state, informing me of
                    the determination of the Spanish government to anticipate payment of the
                    indemnity money in the matter of the “Virginius” by the immediate delivery of
                    the whole of the first installment and of one-half of the second.</p>
                <p>I shall to-morrow call at the treasury department, and, on receiving the money,
                    remit the same immediately to Messrs. Morton, Rose &amp; Co., as instructed by
                    your telegram of the 7th instant, on the best terms attainable at Madrid.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. CUSHING.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d302-a1.xml" xpointer="d302-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d302-a2.xml" xpointer="d302-a2"/>
